Author: loop-bench <loop-bench@localhost>
Date:   Tue Oct 20 17:50:47 2026 +0200

    fix(tools): repair validation build and cover the contract

    CI on the validation commit was red on four checks. Typecheck: import
    Ajv as a named binding so NodeNext resolves the class, not the module
    namespace. Lint: order helpers caller-first, flatten the required-
    property guard, carry cause on the schema-compile error, and restructure
    the acceptance loop and shared providers to the guard shape the rules
    ask for. Changelog: record the change for package consumers.

    Tests: registry.test.ts gains the remaining unit facets - pass-through
    of extra properties, wrong-type rejection without a value leak, register-
    time compile throw, per-call schema for function-valued sources,
    compile-once across ten executes, and the Unknown tool pin - each as one
    grouped assertion, and chatOrchestrator.test.ts drives a rejected call
    through a corrected retry. Docs: README, .specify/spec.md, the tool guide
    and the weather example now state the enforced schema contract; ADR-002
    notes the input-validation slice shipped; the spec cites every statement
    and reads Shipped.

    Relates to #37

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

